    <!-- THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE <Layout>
         breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent
         xml file" error.

         🔴 Buyer__c REMOVED FROM THIS LAYOUT 2026-08-21 (buyer-to-broker-counterparty-change.md).
         SUPERSEDED BY Disposition_Offer__c.Broker__c, WHICH IS DELIBERATELY NOT ON THIS LAYOUT
         EITHER (see that field's own comment - it is machine-stamped, not analyst-entered). User
         decision: "we don't need buyer information, we just need broker contact for disposition
         offers and NDA." Buyer__c the FIELD is NOT deleted - this repo's standing rule is
         additive (add -> repoint -> retire) and a deletion needs its own sequenced wave plus a
         manual Setup erase - only its reachability from this form is removed. Its permission-set
         grants and Buyer_Name__c (the separate free-text field, already removed from this layout
         2026-08-21 below) are untouched by this change; narrowing those was not asked for here.

         BUSINESS FIELDS ADDED 2026-08-20 (UAT gap). Until now this layout was a STUB: it carried
         exactly four fields, Name, OwnerId, CreatedById and LastModifiedById, and not one business
         field. Clicking "+ Log Offer" therefore opened a "New Disposition Offer" modal offering
         only a blank auto number and an Owner picker, so the analyst had nowhere to type the buyer,
         the price, or the terms. Same defect as BOV_Submission__c, found in the same UAT pass.

         WHY IT SURVIVED TO UAT: every read path bypasses layouts. DispositionOfferSelector names
         its columns in SOQL and dispositionCallForOffers renders them itself, so the offer table
         looked complete while the create and detail screens were empty. Nothing in the Jest or Apex
         suites exercises a page layout.

         🔴 A SECOND EXPOSURE THIS CLOSES, AND ONE UAT STEP IT NEEDS. Both
         lwc/dispositionOffer/dispositionOffer.js and
         lwc/dispositionCallForOffers/dispositionCallForOffers.js navigate to standard__objectPage
         actionName 'new' seeding Disposition__c through defaultFieldValues - and Disposition__c
         WAS NOT ON THIS LAYOUT. The create screen renders its inputs from this layout, so there
         was no input for that default to land in, and the analyst could not have set the parent by
         hand either.
         ⚠ WHETHER THE PLATFORM STILL APPLIES A DEFAULT TO A FIELD WITH NO RENDERED INPUT IS NOT
         STATED IN THE defaultFieldValues DOCUMENTATION, AND WAS NOT TESTED HERE. So this is
         recorded as an open risk, not as a finding: if the value was being dropped, every offer
         logged through those buttons is orphaned from its Disposition and existing UAT data needs
         checking. Placing Disposition__c here removes the question either way.
         CONFIRM IN UAT: log one offer through "+ Log Offer" and check the parent is populated. Do
         not assume it was, and do not assume it was not.

         BEHAVIOUR RULES APPLIED, and each Readonly below is deliberate:
         1. NO FORMULA FIELDS EXIST ON THIS OBJECT. All sixteen custom fields were checked in
            objects/Disposition_Offer__c/fields/; none carries a formula element, so rule 1 has
            nothing to bite on here. Every Readonly below is a rule 2 decision, not a type
            constraint.
         2. MACHINE WRITTEN FIELDS ARE Readonly:
            Approval_Status__c is written ONLY by workflows/Disposition_Offer__c.workflow_meta
            Set_Offer_Approval_Approved and Set_Offer_Approval_Rejected, fired as the final actions
            of approvalProcesses/Disposition_Offer__c.Offer_Selection_Approval.
            DispositionOfferTriggerHandler reads exactly that value to accept the offer and advance
            the parent Disposition from Offer Selection to LOI, so a hand edit would move a deal
            without an approval.
            Is_Selected__c is written ONLY by DispositionApprovalService.selectOffer, whose "at most
            one selected offer" guarantee is a property of THAT SERVICE and not of the field: it
            flips the winner on and clears every rival in one exclusive DML. The field itself has no
            uniqueness constraint, so a hand edit produces two selected offers and
            Offer_Selection_Approval, whose entry criterion is Is_Selected__c = true, would then
            match both.
            This is the same reasoning that set Selected_Broker__c to readonly on the Disposition
            FlexiPage yesterday under code review W1, and it is applied consistently here.
            It also MATCHES THE FLS ALREADY IN THE ORG: permissionsets/DPEG_Disposition_Edit grants
            both fields readable=true editable=false, so an Edit behaviour here would have
            advertised a write the persona does not have.
         3. Name stays Readonly. It is an AutoNumber, displayFormat OFFER-{0000}.
         4. Offer_Status__c IS LEFT EDITABLE ON PURPOSE even though DispositionOfferTriggerHandler
            stamps ONE of its values. The handler only writes 'Accepted', and only in the before
            update that follows an approval. Every other transition, Received, Countered and so on,
            is the analyst's to log, so this is not a machine owned field and locking it would
            remove the ability to record a negotiation.

         THE relatedLists BLOCK BELOW IS UNTOUCHED. It carries RelatedProcessHistoryList, which is
         the only route to Recall Approval Request on this object.

         =====================================================================================
         Buyer__c ADDED 2026-08-20 (Workstream D6.1, buyer activity timeline,
         disposition-tranche-2-requirements.md §3). Placed directly after Name/Disposition__c in
         the Information section - this object has NO custom FlexiPage anywhere in force-app
         (see the "SECOND EXPOSURE" note above), so this layout is the ONLY route to
         reachability for this field, unlike NDA__c which also has a Dynamic Forms record page.
         Edit behaviour: the field is analyst-entered and carries no machine-only write path.

         =====================================================================================
         🔴 FORM SIMPLIFICATION, 2026-08-21 (offer-form-and-stage-retirement.md, Request A).
         REMOVED FROM THIS LAYOUT: Buyer_Name__c, NDA_Status__c, Offer_Status__c, and the whole
         "Selection and Approval" section (Is_Selected__c, Approval_Status__c).
         =====================================================================================
         Buyer_Name__c is removed by explicit user instruction. It is NOT retired and NOT
         cleared - DispositionOfferBuyerStampService still writes it in before-context
         in-memory, "NOT FLS-checked" per that class's own header, so layout removal does not
         disable the stamp. lwc/dispositionOffer's offer table still renders it as a column;
         removing it from the FORM does not remove it from that read path. Buyer__c ("Buyer
         Contact") is EXPLICITLY KEPT VISIBLE and Edit, by the same instruction - both fields
         being on the layout was never required, only Buyer_Name__c specifically was asked to be
         hidden.
         NDA_Status__c and Offer_Status__c have no machine writer that a hidden field would
         disable: NDA_Status__c has none at all (confirmed - no Apex, LWC, flow or approval page
         field references it), and Offer_Status__c's only writer
         (DispositionOfferTriggerHandler.stampAcceptedStatus) only ever writes 'Accepted' after
         approval - hiding the field removes the analyst's ability to log intermediate
         negotiation states (Received, Countered, etc.) by hand; the user was told and made the
         call anyway.
         The "Selection and Approval" section is removed in full, not narrowed - it was a
         sibling of two other layoutSections, not itself split into hideable pieces. Both fields
         it carried are already Readonly and editable=false in DPEG_Disposition_Edit and are
         written only by DispositionApprovalService (Is_Selected__c) and the
         Offer_Selection_Approval workflow field updates (Approval_Status__c), neither of which
         reads a layout, so removing the section disables no automation.

         🔴 Offer_Financing_Type__c IS DELIBERATELY NOT HIDDEN, DESPITE BEING ASKED FOR. It is
         read by lwc/dispositionOfferSelect (the Select Offer screen where DPEG picks the
         winning bid) and is an approvalPageField on Offer_Selection_Approval, seen by both
         named approval principals. This layout is the ONLY entry point for this field (no
         FlexiPage exists for this object) - hiding it would make it permanently unenterable and
         both downstream screens would render it blank on every offer created after the change,
         with no error anywhere. The user was told and this field was kept on the form.

         🔴 THE relatedLists BLOCK BELOW IS UNTOUCHED BY THIS CHANGE TOO. It still carries
         RelatedProcessHistoryList, the only route to Recall Approval Request on this object.
         ===================================================================================== -->
